questions.question:
The notifications service sent "Your courier is here" before "A courier accepted your order". The producer sent every event without a key:

```text
$ kafka-console-consumer --bootstrap-server kafka:9092 --topic orders.v1 --from-beginning \
    --property print.partition=true --property print.offset=true | grep o-1842
Partition:3  Offset:5120  {"type":"OrderPlaced","orderId":"o-1842"}
Partition:0  Offset:4987  {"type":"OrderAccepted","orderId":"o-1842"}
Partition:5  Offset:5302  {"type":"CourierAssigned","orderId":"o-1842"}
Partition:1  Offset:5011  {"type":"OrderDelivered","orderId":"o-1842"}
```

Statement: "Kafka delivers a topic's messages in the order they were produced, so the notifications consumer must be reordering them; the fix belongs in the consumer."
